This is a carry step, not a re-run: the synthesis produced last cycle stands, and my work here is to check its grounds against what is actually exposed now, make one small repair in the design's own idiom, and state the result compactly enough that the next invocation can run from it even if the prior body is not re-exposed. The origin artifact is absent, as before.

First, the provenance check. The two artifacts exposed alongside the synthesis — the account as carry.1, the objection as carry.2 — contain, under the same local ids and with matching substance, every record of theirs that the synthesis cites under their earlier labels: from the account, the underspecification conjecture, the churn critique, the low-confidence reading of avoidance, the trial mechanics, the goodwill stance, the two open problems, and the charitable-reading objection (c1-c3, cm1-cm4, p1, p2, o1); from the objection, the incomplete-contract claim, the self-report gap, the over-promise objection, the exploitability and ledger-tension objections, the two structural objections to the entrance, the record-as-fairness-instrument use, and the two problems (n1, n2, ob1-ob5, u1, pr1, pr2). So the synthesis's grounds in those two inputs are intact and re-verified from what I can currently see. The third input it used — the rival response, cited inside it as response.2#r1-r7 — is not exposed in this invocation; its content (the over-coupling conjecture, the decoupling menu, the stand-down-first ordering, the discriminating checks, the sequencing principle) survives only as reported within the synthesis's own text. One further nuance: the account is exposed here in commitments view only, so the one clause the synthesis quoted from its body prose — 'without any fairness negotiation at all' — is traceable to the objection's quotation of it; nothing in the plan turns on the exact wording, since the repair was accepted on the objection's terms and the commitment it revises (cm2) is itself exposed. Practical upshot: the plan is executable as it stands, but the ordering dispute (j1) and the framing contest (pB) must not be relitigated without first re-exposing the rival.

The standing plan, restated. Diagnosis held as conjecture: the disputes more plausibly come from underspecified agreements compounded by schedule churn than from unwillingness (carry.1#c1, c2); why the friend avoids the conversations is unresolved across four disjuncts (p1); whether the work is distributed unfairly is unknown (p2). Selection criterion: with the diagnosis unresolved, prefer moves that are useful or at worst harmless under every live hypothesis and that generate evidence discriminating among them (k1). Three repairs to the written-trial mechanics, all drawn from the objection: contested done-lines are rewritten together rather than litigated — the no-blame rule extended from misses to lines (k2); the record's legitimate uses are stated — open use by anyone, no private tallies, fairness raised at a standing venue rather than against a threshold (k3); the revision meeting opens with a claimed-versus-completed totals review, the fairness floor (k4). Entrance replaced: not the process-first one-to-one, which rested on the plan's weakest claim, was itself an instance of the avoided genre, and was the plan's only door (ob4, ob5); instead, co-own the proposal with the approachable third flatmate, open the artifact asynchronously and opt-in with an explicit stand-down line co-signed where possible, and reserve the one-to-one until the opt-in window has shown something (k5). Run as a probe: three observations — where disputes recur (claims, done-lines, or neither), whether the avoider engages with a de-centered opt-in format, whether the artifact is used when nobody pushes — and the standing review branches on them: continue the mechanics, open the held decoupling menu, address fairness from the totals, or hand over convening (k6). Rejected, with its components preserved: stand-down-and-decouple as the fixed first move — it concedes the convener hypothesis before testing it, needs the very agreement capacity it diagnoses as scarce, and is less reversible than a two-week opt-in trial (j1).

One repair at this carry, in the design's own idiom. The ledger-use rule as worded — the record used only at the standing review — sits against an entrance that relies on continuous operational use: people must post tasks, claim against shifts, mark completions and re-claim misses all week. A design whose founding insight is that rules relocate ambiguity rather than abolish it should not ship an ambiguous meta-rule about itself: left implicit, 'you consulted the record mid-week' becomes the first seed dispute of the new system. The record rule therefore now names two uses: operational — open and continuous, handled at short check-ins — and evaluative — totals, fairness, the branch decision — reserved for the dated standing review; no private tallies of either kind; check-in frequency is set by the flatmates at proposal time, the revision date unchanged (d2 below).

Carried open, deliberately: the cause of the avoidance (pA); the framing contest between agreement failure and over-coupling, which the probe rather than prose is to settle (pB); the third-flatmate caveat, with its fallback to reserved one-to-ones and no shared artifact until one is secured (pC); the noted weakness of domain ownership — it binds a standard to a person and so inherits the churn objection — should the menu ever open (j2); and the new provenance gap above (d4).

What I would defend unconditionally is unchanged: the criterion and the probes, not any framing. None of us can see this flat.